<article class="env-lemma" id="0CP3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CP3">Lemma <span data-tag="0CP3">67.16.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a separated morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $V \subset Y$ be an open subspace such that $V \to Y$ is quasi-compact. Let $s : V \to X$ be a morphism such that $f \circ s = \text{id}_ V$. Let $Y'$ be the scheme theoretic image of $s$. Then $Y' \to Y$ is an isomorphism over $V$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/03KS" data-tag="03KS">67.8.9</a> the morphism $s : V \to X$ is quasi-compact. Hence the construction of the scheme theoretic image $Y'$ of $s$ commutes with restriction to opens by Lemma <a href="/tag/082Z" data-tag="082Z">67.16.3</a>. In particular, we see that $Y' \cap f^{-1}(V)$ is the scheme theoretic image of a section of the separated morphism $f^{-1}(V) \to V$. Since a section of a separated morphism is a closed immersion (Lemma <a href="/tag/03KP" data-tag="03KP">67.4.7</a>), we conclude that $Y' \cap f^{-1}(V) \to V$ is an isomorphism as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>